flowchart TB
  accTitle: Optimize a stage, then recompute the whole path
  accDescr: The illustrative sequential request parses for two milliseconds, fetches for forty, computes for eight and serializes for three, totaling fifty-three. Halving only computation to four milliseconds reduces the total to forty-nine. All stages are sequential with no queueing or overlap.
  A["Parse: 2 ms"] --> B["Remote fetch: 40 ms"]
  B --> C["Compute: 8 ms<br/>Optimized: 4 ms"]
  C --> D["Serialize: 3 ms"]
  D --> E["Original total: 53 ms<br/>Optimized total: 49 ms"]
  class B neutral;
  class C control;
  class E success;

  classDef control fill:#F5F3FF,stroke:#7C3AED,color:#111827;
  classDef neutral fill:#F3F4F6,stroke:#4B5563,color:#111827;
  classDef success fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#15803D,color:#111827;
  classDef pending fill:#FFFBEB,stroke:#B45309,color:#111827;
  classDef failure fill:#FEE2E2,stroke:#B91C1C,color:#111827;

